      "problem": "Let $a=⟨3,-4,5⟩$ and $b=⟨2,-6,1⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 2+(-4)\\cdot (-6)+5\\cdot 1}{{2}^{2}+(-6)^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{41}⟨2,-6,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{70}{41},-\\frac{210}{41},\\frac{35}{41}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
